1
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:04,580
- Hey.         - Hey.

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,750
Sorry I'm late. Did I miss anything?

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,670
Joey stuffing fifteen Oreos in his mouth.

4
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,010
Fifteen?

5
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:14,170
Your personal best! Ha, ha.

6
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,430
Where were you?

7
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,770
On a date.

8
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:24,440
I met this girl on a train going to a museum upstate.

9
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,560
- Which museum?     - How'd you meet her?

10
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,860
No. Answer his.

11
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,940
We were at the back of the train.

12
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:36,530
I sat near the door so she'd have to pass by me...

13
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:40,740
...if she wanted to switch cars. She was totally at my mercy.

14
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:44,250
Were you so late because you were burying this woman?

15
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:47,040
I'm late because she lives in Poughkeepsie.

16
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:50,630
She seems great, but she's two and a half hours away.

17
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:54,260
How can she be great if she's from Poughkeepsie? Ha-ha-ha.

18
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:57,800
That joke would have killed in Albany.

19
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,720
Done! I did it.

20
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,430
Who's stupid now?

21
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:57,440
Look! They're lighting the big Christmas tree tonight.

22
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:59,660
Um, that paper is two weeks old.

23
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:04,330
Who keeps leaving old newspapers in the trash?

24
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,620
I really wanted to take Kathy to this.

25
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:12,960
At least you have somebody to miss stuff with.

26
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,380
I hate being alone this time of year.

27
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,760
Next it's Valentine's Day...

28
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:19,880
...then my birthday, then bang!

29
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:22,890
Then they're lighting that damn tree again.

30
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:26,600
I want somebody!

31
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:32,310
You know, I want a man!

32
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:41,360
It doesn't even have to be a big relationship. Just a fling!

33
00:02:41,610 --> 00:02:44,740
I didn't think girls ever just wanted a fling.

34
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:49,000
Let me tell you, it's been a long time since I've been flung.

35
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,670
I know what I'm giving you for Christmas.

36
00:02:56,170 --> 00:02:59,010
There are nice guys in my office. Want me to set you up?

37
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,420
Yeah.

38
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:04,800
I've been single a long time. Why haven't you offered before?

39
00:03:05,050 --> 00:03:07,680
I have a girlfriend. I'm happy.

40
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:12,560
I no longer go out of my way to stop others from being happy.

41
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:14,730
Okay.

42
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:16,520
No accountants.

43
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:20,190
And no one from "legal." I don't like boring jobs.

44
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:23,990
And Ross was what? A lion tamer?

45
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,490
What's wrong, Mon?

46
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:32,120
Everybody at work still hates me.

47
00:03:32,330 --> 00:03:33,500
I was making headway.

48
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:36,920
Everyone was smiling at me, and then I get off work...

49
00:03:37,130 --> 00:03:40,340
...and find out they wrote this on my chef's hat.

50
00:03:44,050 --> 00:03:48,140
Maybe they meant to write "Quiet, Bitch."

51
00:03:52,810 --> 00:03:54,600
What's the matter?

52
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:57,440
Fine! Just trying to be nice.

53
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:02,820
I haven't been picked on this much since kindergarten.

54
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:07,030
And they brought in someone from junior high to do the see-saw with me.

55
00:04:09,790 --> 00:04:11,540
Aw.

56
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:16,830
They're trying to make me quit. If it were any other job, I would.

57
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
But I've waited for this my whole life.

58
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:23,050
Wait, you're the boss. Yell at them. Or fire them!

59
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:27,930
I would love to, but I can't. I'm not good at confrontation.

60
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,510
You know what you can do?

61
00:04:29,810 --> 00:04:33,020
I read about this director, Orson Welles...

62
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:37,230
...who, at the beginning, would hire somebody just to fire them.

63
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:40,190
Then they would all know who was boss.

64
00:04:42,070 --> 00:04:44,530
I'm not doing anything. Why not fire me?

65
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:49,200
It's a good idea. Can you waiter?

66
00:04:49,370 --> 00:04:51,120
Good enough to get fired.

67
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,910
All right. You're hired!

68
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,540
Hey!

69
00:04:56,420 --> 00:05:01,420
That's why I got fired last week! Does Orson Welles direct commercials?

70
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,720
Yes.

71
00:05:17,770 --> 00:05:20,770
I say, Drew? Are you seeing anybody right now?

72
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:23,070
I'm not asking for me.

73
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:26,990
I'm not gay. I'm not asking you out.

74
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,860
I'm not gay.

75
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:31,280
I didn't think you were gay.

76
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:33,040
I do now.

77
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:38,420
My friend, Rachel, wants to be set up.

78
00:05:38,790 --> 00:05:41,210
I just got out of a big relationship.

79
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,380
I'm not looking to get serious.

80
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:46,970
That's okay. A fling might be all right with her.

81
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:51,550
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Is this "Hot Rachel" that you took to the Christmas Party?

82
00:05:51,970 --> 00:05:54,310
By the way, that is her full name.

83
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,730
Wow! I'm free for her.

84
00:05:56,930 --> 00:05:59,390
Wait, I didn't say I wasn't free.

85
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,440
Let's talk it over at the Ranger game.

86
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:05,820
Hold on. I just got a box of Cubans.

87
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:08,530
I'll bring them by your office at 5.

88
00:06:09,450 --> 00:06:13,620
That's a little later than I usually stay, but sure.

89
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:17,750
Before the game, we could enjoy some eight-year-old Basil Haydens.

90
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:20,830
I don't know what that is, but let's!

91
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:29,630
I'm writing a holiday song for everyone. Do you want to hear it?

92
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,800
- Yeah!     - Yes!

93
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:34,680
Okay.

94
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:39,310
Happy Hanukkah, Monica

95
00:06:41,350 --> 00:06:44,480
May your Christmas be snowy, Joey

96
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:47,530
Happy New Year, Chandler and Ross

97
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:51,030
Spin the dreidel, Rachel

98
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:56,280
- Pheebs, that's great!     - Oh, yay!

99
00:06:56,540 --> 00:07:00,410
But you know, uh, Rachel doesn't rhyme with dreidel.

100
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:05,500
I know, but it's so hard. Nothing rhymes with your stupid name!

101
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:09,010
What are you talking about? Lots of things rhyme with Rachel:

102
00:07:09,260 --> 00:07:13,550
Bagel, mail, jail, bail, cable.

103
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,220
Maypole.

104
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,350
All good. Thanks.

105
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:23,770
Um, do you, maybe, have a nickname that's easier to rhyme?

106
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,270
- Didn't your dad call you "Pumpkin"?     - Oh, yeah.

107
00:07:27,610 --> 00:07:30,070
But did he ever call you "Budolph"?

108
00:07:33,570 --> 00:07:35,240
- Hello, children.     - Hey.

109
00:07:36,030 --> 00:07:38,950
Have I got the 50 guys for you!

110
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:40,750
Really?

111
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,750
I showed them your picture.

112
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:45,960
Guys are throwing themselves at me and giving me stuff.

113
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:47,960
- Knicks tonight?     - Where are the seats?

114
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:50,170
Wherever! I've got 20.

115
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,260
Will I like any of these guys?

116
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:56,390
You know, I'm going to, uh...

117
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:59,060
...play the field a little bit more.     - Chandler...

118
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:03,440
Guys are signing over their 401 Ks to me.

119
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,770
You work with robots?

120
00:08:10,530 --> 00:08:11,570
Yes.

121
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:18,070
One guy, Patrick, you'll like him. He's nice, funny and a swimmer.

122
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:19,990
I like swimmers' bodies.

123
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:23,000
His dad made the magnetic strip on credit cards.

124
00:08:23,790 --> 00:08:24,830
I like credit cards!

125
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:28,040
I'm not bad at this!

126
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:30,920
- What does he do?     - He works in fine foods.

127
00:08:31,210 --> 00:08:35,590
- You have a fine foods division?     - It's a big company...

128
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:38,890
Now, wait a second. You make food and robots?

129
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:43,730
No, the robots just work for them.

130
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:46,980
All right, I'm going to work.

131
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,520
Does anybody have a problem with that?

132
00:08:49,770 --> 00:08:51,860
Yeah, lady. I do!

133
00:08:52,110 --> 00:08:53,150
I got a problem!

134
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,490
I'll give you a problem!

135
00:08:56,030 --> 00:08:57,780
What will you do? Fire me?

136
00:08:57,990 --> 00:09:00,450
You bet your ass I'll fire you!

137
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:02,410
See you later.

138
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:10,460
I should go. I've got a date.

139
00:09:10,710 --> 00:09:11,840
With who?

140
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:15,130
You know the girl who lives in Poughkeepsie?

141
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:16,630
Not her.

142
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:19,220
This is someone else.

143
00:09:19,470 --> 00:09:21,930
I can't decide between the two.

144
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:26,600
The one from Poughkeepsie, though two hours away, is pretty...

145
00:09:26,810 --> 00:09:29,270
...really smart and a lot of fun.

146
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:33,480
But this other girl, she lives right uptown.

147
00:09:35,650 --> 00:09:37,860
She's just as pretty.

148
00:09:38,070 --> 00:09:39,820
I guess she's smart.

149
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,370
She's not fun.

150
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:47,080
If she's no fun, why date her at all?

151
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:51,040
I want to give her a chance. She lives so close.

152
00:09:51,710 --> 00:09:55,920
And, at the end of the date, she said something that...

153
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:59,220
...if she was kidding, was very funny.

154
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:04,470
If she wasn't kidding, she's not fun. She's stupid and racist.

155
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:08,350
- Hey.     - Hey.

156
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:11,690
How was your first day at the restaurant?

157
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,730
Damn!

158
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:22,070
- Hey.     - Hey.

159
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,370
What happened to your fancy jacket?

160
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:26,240
They baked it.

161
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:27,790
I can't take this anymore.

162
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,170
- I'm going to fire you tonight.     - You got it. Oh, oh!

163
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:32,710
What are you doing?

164
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:35,630
You're still on fire there.

165
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,170
I think you got it!

166
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:47,140
Chandler, you have the best taste in men.

167
00:10:48,310 --> 00:10:50,440
Like father, like son.

168
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:54,360
Patrick and I had such a great time last night!

169
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:56,900
This could, maybe, get serious.

170
00:10:57,360 --> 00:11:01,110
I thought you weren't looking for serious. Just a fling?

171
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,990
Well, you know, possibly.

172
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:09,790
You didn't tell him that, though, right?

173
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:12,830
Uh, no?

174
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:17,590
You told this guy that I was looking for a fling?

175
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:20,090
- You don't tell him that!     - Why not?

176
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:22,590
I'd be thrilled if some hot girl...

177
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:23,800
I see.

178
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:28,810
You telling him I want a fling and me putting out...

179
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:31,940
...he's so going to get the wrong idea!

180
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,400
Joey, could you pass the cheese?

181
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:42,280
I'd prefer you didn't call me Joey.

182
00:11:42,530 --> 00:11:45,910
I thought it might be fun to try out a cool nickname.

183
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,120
Hey, Dragon!

184
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:52,370
Here's your tips from Monday and Tuesday.

185
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,290
There's $300 in this one.

186
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:58,000
People get generous around the holidays.

187
00:11:58,210 --> 00:12:01,590
And it never hurts to wear tight trousers.

188
00:12:04,050 --> 00:12:06,970
Could the waiters listen to the specials?

189
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:11,020
There's Chilean sea bass with a mango relish...

190
00:12:11,810 --> 00:12:13,270
Why is nobody writing these?

191
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:14,810
We can remember them.

192
00:12:15,150 --> 00:12:19,190
Because you'll make up fake specials and make me cook them?

193
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:22,150
Sure, that too.

194
00:12:23,530 --> 00:12:27,910
Forget the specials for a minute. Um, here's the thing...

195
00:12:29,410 --> 00:12:31,490
For the last two weeks I have, uh...

196
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:36,330
...tried hard to create a positive atmosphere.

197
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:38,000
Can't hear you!

198
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,920
Positive atmosphere.

199
00:12:42,130 --> 00:12:44,760
But I've had it up to here.

200
00:12:48,390 --> 00:12:51,510
From now on, it is going to be my way...

201
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:55,390
...or the highway. All right?

202
00:12:56,310 --> 00:12:59,150
Does anybody have a problem with that?

203
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,370
Hey, new guy.

204
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:13,830
I said, does anybody have a problem with that?

205
00:13:15,290 --> 00:13:16,960
No, ma'am.

206
00:13:18,710 --> 00:13:21,090
He has a name. It's Dragon.

207
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:25,880
You want to know your name? Check your hat.

208
00:13:26,130 --> 00:13:28,430
We did the hat, right?

209
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:35,890
- What the hell just happened?     - I am so sorry.

210
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,520
I was going to do it.

211
00:13:37,730 --> 00:13:41,360
But I was standing there with $327 in one hand...

212
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:44,900
...and $238 in the other. And I was thinking...

213
00:13:45,110 --> 00:13:47,570
...it's been a long time since I had...

214
00:13:48,990 --> 00:13:51,620
...327 plus $238!

215
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:56,750
We had a deal! It's why you're here. I've got to fire you!

216
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,420
And I got to pay rent!

217
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,590
How about you don't fire me.

218
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:06,420
Instead, I stay. I gain their trust.

219
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:10,010
They'll listen to the nice things I say about you.

220
00:14:11,430 --> 00:14:12,600
What nice things?

221
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:16,310
Nothing yet. They hate you, and I want to fit in.

222
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:20,650
Happy Hanukkah, Chandler and Monica, Merry, merry...

223
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,900
You know what, Pheebs?

224
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:25,900
I'm not Jewish so...

225
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:29,530
Ross doesn't decorate his tree with floss...

226
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:31,780
...but he's not complaining.

227
00:14:35,790 --> 00:14:37,410
Bad dream?

228
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,250
I wasn't sleeping.

229
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:42,960
What was Phoebe's song about?

230
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:47,090
It's the one with the cat.

231
00:14:48,670 --> 00:14:51,680
I got to go. I've got another date.

232
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:53,640
Did you pick one yet?

233
00:14:53,890 --> 00:14:57,770
It turns out the one from uptown was making a joke.

234
00:14:58,350 --> 00:15:02,150
It was a different joke. It wasn't that funny.

235
00:15:03,190 --> 00:15:04,650
So I'm still torn.

236
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:06,980
You don't like the one from uptown.

237
00:15:07,150 --> 00:15:09,990
And you're exhausted from dating Poughkeepsie.

238
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,070
Just end them both!

239
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,990
Go to Poughkeepsie and break up with her.

240
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,990
Then break up with uptown.

241
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:19,830
By the time you get home, you're done!

242
00:15:21,330 --> 00:15:23,250
You're right. Thank you.

243
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:27,590
I had a similar problem when I lived in Prague.

244
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:31,670
- Prague?     - So much you don't know.

245
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:46,020
Chandler?

246
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,650
Patrick just, uh, ended things with me.

247
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:53,950
Did you or didn't you tell him I wanted a serious relationship?

248
00:15:54,450 --> 00:15:56,240
I did! I absolutely did!

249
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,240
You idiot!

250
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,750
I'm sure you're right. But why?

251
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:05,880
You don't tell a guy that you want a serious relationship.

252
00:16:06,250 --> 00:16:08,040
Now you scared him away!

253
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:11,260
I am sorry. I am so sorry.

254
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:14,470
You should never be allowed to talk to people!

255
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:16,930
I know, I know!

256
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:20,140
Now I'm right back where I started.

257
00:16:20,390 --> 00:16:21,890
This sucks!

258
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:24,140
Being alone sucks!

259
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:26,730
You'll meet somebody.

260
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,900
You're a great catch!

261
00:16:29,150 --> 00:16:33,900
When I told those guys about you, I didn't have to lie once.

262
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,660
- Really?     - Yeah.

263
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:40,410
You graduated magna cum laude, right?

264
00:16:41,330 --> 00:16:42,370
No.

265
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:44,580
It doesn't matter.

266
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:51,250
I got tickets to the Ranger game. You want to come with me?

267
00:16:52,170 --> 00:16:54,340
Cute guys in little shorts?

268
00:16:54,550 --> 00:16:55,840
Sure.

269
00:16:57,300 --> 00:17:02,100
Actually, it's a hockey team. Angry Canadians with no teeth.

270
00:17:02,310 --> 00:17:04,730
That sounds fun too. Thank you.

271
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,060
Okay.

272
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:12,230
Have you ever been with a woman?

273
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:14,990
What?

274
00:17:15,150 --> 00:17:17,360
What is the matter with you?

275
00:17:17,610 --> 00:17:21,200
There is no good time to ask that question.

276
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:28,460
The station is Poughkeepsie. Poughkeepsie!

277
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:33,380
Ross?

278
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,010
Wake up!

279
00:17:38,430 --> 00:17:41,680
Ross? Ross! Ross!

280
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:46,640
I need more swordfish.

281
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:51,400
- Can you get me more swordfish?     - I don't speak English.

282
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:53,520
You just did.

283
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:56,240
I don't know what to tell you.

284
00:17:57,450 --> 00:17:58,950
Fine.

285
00:18:08,750 --> 00:18:10,630
Very funny.

286
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,090
Let me out, please.

287
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:15,670
Come on, I'm cold!

288
00:18:18,010 --> 00:18:20,890
And covered in marinara sauce!

289
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:22,470
Let me out!

290
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:28,980
You found that handle, did you?

291
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:33,900
- It's not funny.     - Well, that's not true.

292
00:18:36,150 --> 00:18:39,400
I'm a good person. And I'm a good chef.

293
00:18:39,610 --> 00:18:43,740
And I don't deserve to have marinara sauce all over me!

294
00:18:43,950 --> 00:18:46,660
If you want me to quit this bad then...

295
00:18:46,830 --> 00:18:48,700
Hey. Chef Geller?

296
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:51,460
You know that speech you made?

297
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:53,920
I got a problem with it!

298
00:18:56,590 --> 00:18:58,840
- You do?     - You bet I do!

299
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:03,430
I just, uh, wasn't listening then, that's all.

300
00:19:04,970 --> 00:19:08,980
If you want a problem, I'll give you a problem!

301
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:12,150
What are you going to do? Fire me?

302
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:15,900
You bet I'll fire you! Get out of my kitchen!

303
00:19:16,570 --> 00:19:18,360
Get out!

304
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:22,780
All right.

305
00:19:23,910 --> 00:19:25,740
Anybody else got a problem?

306
00:19:25,950 --> 00:19:27,990
How about you, chuckles?

307
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:29,950
You think this is funny now?

308
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,210
No.

309
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:36,840
What if I dance covered in sauce? You think it's funny?

310
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,590
No, it's really good.

311
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:43,430
Take those salads to table four.

312
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:45,430
And you, get the swordfish!

313
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:47,180
And you!

314
00:19:47,510 --> 00:19:49,180
Get a haircut!

315
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:56,940
Last stop, Montreal. The stop is Montreal!

316
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:01,280
What?

317
00:20:05,660 --> 00:20:08,990
I bet myself that you had beautiful eyes.

318
00:20:09,290 --> 00:20:11,700
Now that I see them, I win!

319
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:15,960
What?

320
00:20:17,170 --> 00:20:20,420
We're at my stop. Would you like to have coffee?

321
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,340
Are we really in Montreal?

322
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:27,970
Yes, we are.

323
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,680
So coffee?

324
00:20:31,930 --> 00:20:33,430
Coffee sounds great.

325
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:37,360
Wait.

326
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:39,520
So you live in Montreal?

327
00:20:39,730 --> 00:20:43,440
No, but it's only a two-hour ferry ride to Nova Scotia.

328
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:49,490
I should have thought about my wife and kids...

329
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:52,040
...before I talked back to Chef Geller.

330
00:20:53,410 --> 00:20:54,460
Thanks.

331
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:58,960
It will be a lean Christmas at the Dragon house this year.

332
00:21:02,010 --> 00:21:03,460
Enough!

333
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,390
Lean, lean, lean!

334
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,680
Went to the store Sat on Santa's lap

335
00:21:13,850 --> 00:21:16,940
Asked him to bring my friends All kinds of crap

336
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:21,900
Said all you need is To write them a song

337
00:21:22,230 --> 00:21:26,070
Now you haven't heard it yet So don't try to sing along

338
00:21:26,950 --> 00:21:29,370
No, don't sing along

339
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:32,790
Monica, Monica

340
00:21:33,120 --> 00:21:36,250
Have a happy Hanukkah

341
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:40,130
Saw Santa Claus

342
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:43,800
He said hello to Ross

343
00:21:45,010 --> 00:21:47,880
And please tell Joey

344
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:51,390
Christmas will be snowy

345
00:21:52,930 --> 00:21:55,890
And Rachel and Chandler

346
00:22:01,190 --> 00:22:03,400
Happy holidays, everybody!

